  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient Urban Centres and Surrounds in the Mekong subregion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The investment aims to provide a practical demonstration of how nature-based solutions (NbS) (e.g., wetlands, catchment protection, green walls, and multifunctional parks) can be better integrated with conventional traditional infrastructure (e.g., levee banks, pipelines, treatment plants) to help mitigate problems caused by urbanisation and induced by climate change. The program uses water management as a catalyst to promote urban climate resilience in four countries of the lower Mekong region &#x2013; Cambodia, Lao PDR, Thailand, and Viet Nam. The end of program outcomes are: a) the value of hybrid NbS is accepted by Mekong partners, b) the foundations for upscaling are put in place, and c) partnerships and capacity for achieving scaling are established, with gender equality and disability and social inclusion principles is a cross-cutting focus.</narrative>
  </description>
